node_modules/
data/settings.json
# Photos of a real person, and other channels' thumbnails. Neither is ours to
# hand out in a repo, and the second is not ours to relicense at all. The
# folders keep a README saying what to put in them.
#
# This rule is what makes this repository publishable. scripts/check-release.mjs
# enforces it against history as well as the working tree, because a purge is
# not something you get to do twice.
# Deliberately not a list of extensions. A rule naming jpg/png/webp misses the
# .heic an iPhone actually hands you, and that is the accident that happens.
brand/**
!brand/**/
!brand/**/README.md

# The editable master of the product mark. Nothing in the app reads it, it is
# the only asset carrying the machine's account name in its metadata, and MIT
# would hand strangers the right to redistribute a modified brand mark. The
# exported PNGs and SVGs in logo/ are what anyone running this actually needs.
logo/*.ai
logo/*.eps
logo/*.psd
# Guest research: names real people with commercial notes about them.
# data/suggestions.example.json shows the shape.
data/suggestions.json
data/channel-cache.json
data/chatgpt-profile/
data/usage.json
projects/
scripts/*.log
*.log
demo/
scripts/runner-debug.png
# Built by scripts/build-handoff.mjs. It carries host photos on purpose, so it
# must never be tracked here. handoff.config.json names a real person.
handoff/
handoff.zip
handoff.config.json
